			<div class="content" id="post-content-4812099">
									

<blockquote>
<p><em>[&#8230;] The more accurate the map, the more it resembles the territory. The most accurate map possible would be the territory, and thus would be perfectly accurate and perfectly useless. The tale is the map that is the territory.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>- Neil Gaiman, <em>American Gods</em></p>
<p>In late 2007, the people of Bikini Atoll lost a lawsuit against the U.S. Government for its refusal to pay reparations for their displacement due to American nuclear testing on their land. This is about that, sort of. More broadly, it's about homesickness, and immigration, and not having somewhere to return to- but it's also under 500 words long, so I'd rather not get <em>too</em> far ahead of myself there.</p>
<p>This piece took about three hours from start to finish, and was written on impulse in a single sitting. Thanks for reading!</p>
<p>Edit: It seems some key elements of the anomaly aren't quite as clear to some readers as I would have hoped they'd be- if you're one if them, hopefully my replies to the earlier comments in the discussion will clear some of that up for you!</p>

