<p>The continued presence of SCP-5146 within <strong>the</strong> area of the Pacific Islands Territory is to be verified bimonthly via standard checks of the Foundation's routinely updated mapping satellite footage.</p>
</blockquote>
<ul>
<li>I don't think &quot;the&quot; is used properly in this sentence. I can tell by context that it refers to &quot;the area that it is in&quot;, but I think &quot;its&quot; would work better here.</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>The continued presence of SCP-5146 within <strong>its</strong> area of the Pacific Islands Territory is to be verified bimonthly via standard checks of the Foundation's routinely updated mapping satellite footage.</p>
</blockquote>
<ul>
<li>Also, bimonthly is ambiguous, meaning twice a month or every two months. I think an organization like the SCPF would avoid using it for this reason.</li>
</ul>
<p>These aren't a big deal, just some things that caught my eye.</p>
